        "category": "offensive",
        "description": {
            "value": "<p><em>The Art of the Libra Tonfa.</em></p><p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per round</p><p><strong>Requirements</strong> You are wielding both @UUID[Compendium.isaacs-hb-pf2e.saint-class-features.Item.Libra Tonfa (Right)] and @UUID[Compendium.isaacs-hb-pf2e.saint-class-features.Item.Libra Tonfa (Left)]</p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> A melee attack against you critically fails</p><hr /><p>While wielding both Tonfa you gain the <strong>parry</strong> bonus (+1 circumstance to AC) with <strong>no action spent</strong>.</p><p>When the trigger is met, Strike the attacker with a Tonfa; this Strike does not increase your multiple attack penalty.</p><p><strong>Greater (8th level)</strong> The reaction triggers on any <strong>miss</strong>, and the parry bonus becomes <strong>+2</strong> and also applies to <strong>Reflex saves</strong>.</p><p><strong>Perfect (14th level)</strong> You gain <strong>one additional reaction each round</strong>, usable only for The Turning Guard &mdash; which is the second use per round below.</p><hr /><p>Granted by @UUID[Compendium.isaacs-hb-pf2e.saint-class-features.Item.Libra — the Weapons]. Target the attacker and use this; the counter-Strike is rolled outside your multiple attack penalty and followed through to its damage.</p>"
        },
